solution_steps:
on the ellipse such that $AB$ passes through $F = (1,0).$  Let $P = (p,0).$

Let $\angle APF = \angle BPF = \theta.$  Then $\angle APB = 180^\circ - 2 \theta.$

[asy]
unitsize(2 cm);

pair A, B, F, P;
path ell = xscale(sqrt(2))*Circle((0,0),1);

F = (1,0);
A = (sqrt(2)*Cos(80),Sin(80));
B = intersectionpoint(interp(A,F,0.1)--interp(A,F,5),ell);
P = (2,0);

draw(ell);
draw(A--B);
draw(A--P--B);
draw(F--P);

