First, we distribute each term:
\begin{align*}
4(x - x^3) - 3(x^2 - x^3 + x^5) + 2(4x^2 - x^9) &= 4x - 4x^3 - 3x^2 + 3x^3 - 3x^5 + 2(4x^2 - x^9) \\
&= 4x - 4x^3 - 3x^2 + 3x^3 - 3x^5 + 8x^2 - 2x^9.
\end{align*}
Next, we combine like terms:
\begin{align*}
4x - 4x^3 - 3x^2 + 3x^3 - 3x^5 + 8x^2 - 2x^9 &= (4x - 3x^2) + (-4x^3 + 3x^3) + (-3x^5 + 8x^2) - 2x^9 \\
&= 4x - 3x^2 + (-x^3) + (-3x^5 + 8x^2) - 2x^9 \\
&= -2x^9 - 3x^5 + 5x^2 + 4x - x^3.
\end{align*}
Finally, we look at the coefficient of $x^2$, which is $\boxed{5}$.
The answer is: 5

